# Obiter runs with none of these set. Every integration falls back to a local
# path, so `npm run dev` gives you the full loop on a laptop with no accounts.
# Fill them in before recording the demo: the submission has to run the real
# model path and the real database, not the offline compiler and the in-process
# journal.
#
# lib/config.ts is the only file in the app that reads any of these. Nothing
# here carries a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so nothing here can reach a browser.

# Which compiler and which store run behind lib/adapters.ts. Anything that is
# not exactly "real" is treated as fake, which replays fixtures/precedent/ with
# no key and keeps the close journal in process memory.
ADAPTER_MODE=fake

# Postgres, from the Neon dashboard: Project -> Connection Details -> pooled
# connection string, with ?sslmode=require on the end. Empty means the close
# journal lives in memory and does not survive a server restart.
DATABASE_URL=

# Which close the journal rows belong to. A label you choose, not a secret.
# Change it to start a fresh close without touching the existing rows.
OBITER_CLOSE_ID=halden-2026-08

# Anthropic. The precedent compiler calls Claude once per controller decision,
# with the precedent schema enforced as a tool definition.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com -> Settings -> API keys.
# Only read when ADAPTER_MODE=real. In that mode, without a key Obiter tries
# your local `claude` CLI and then the deterministic compiler in
# lib/precedent.ts.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to claude-opus-5.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# Optional. The Anthropic Messages endpoint. Change it only to point at a
# gateway you run yourself; the default is Anthropic's own host.
ANTHROPIC_URL=https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages

# Dodo Payments, test mode. Drives the live settlement feed on the close screen.
# Get a test key at https://app.dodopayments.com -> Developer -> API keys, with
# the environment switch set to test mode. Without it the feed serves the three
# fixture settlements in lib/dodo.ts.
DODO_PAYMENTS_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to the Dodo test host. Point this at the live host only
# when you actually mean to read production money.
DODO_PAYMENTS_API_BASE=https://test.dodopayments.com

# VERCEL is not a settable key and there is deliberately no line for it below.
# The platform sets it to "1" on every Vercel build and every Vercel runtime.
# lib/config.ts reads it once, as RUNNING_ON_VERCEL, and the only thing that
# depends on it is the local `claude` CLI rung in lib/agent.ts: the binary is
# not installed on Vercel, so the spawn probe is skipped there. Setting it by
# hand in .env.local would tell a laptop it is a deploy and cost you that rung.
